1
00:00:00,001 --> 00:00:05,005
(Suddenly showing off their talent)

2
00:00:06,099 --> 00:00:07,966
- Scream, scream
- Ugh, this is exhausting

3
00:00:07,966 --> 00:00:08,883
Oooohhhhh

4
00:00:10,844 --> 00:00:12,679
Hello, everyone

5
00:00:13,347 --> 00:00:13,931
Hah

6
00:00:14,681 --> 00:00:15,432
Aah

7
00:00:15,432 --> 00:00:18,435
I’m here again today to do
another brutally tough part-time job

8
00:00:18,435 --> 00:00:21,187
(Respect)
It feels like watching a Workdol YouTube

9
00:00:21,187 --> 00:00:23,690
Let's see out the supporters
who came out here today

10
00:00:23,690 --> 00:00:25,942
to support Jiwon!

11
00:00:25,942 --> 00:00:26,860
Part-time job supporters

12
00:00:26,860 --> 00:00:27,777
We said we’d do this together

13
00:00:27,777 --> 00:00:28,570
Just a second

14
00:00:28,571 --> 00:00:31,489
(Already out of sync from the start)
- Just a second
- One, two, three

15
00:00:31,489 --> 00:00:31,948
Part-time job

16
00:00:31,948 --> 00:00:32,532
supporters

17
00:00:32,532 --> 00:00:33,283
BABYMONSTER

18
00:00:33,283 --> 00:00:35,243
Okay, sunbae, one more time please

19
00:00:35,243 --> 00:00:39,080
(Rora/ Chiquita/ BABYMONSTER)
We’re BABYMONSTER,
here to help out for the part-time job

20
00:00:39,080 --> 00:00:41,374
From what I heard,

21
00:00:41,374 --> 00:00:42,709
you two have a lot of special talents

22
00:00:42,709 --> 00:00:46,046
(Korea Got Talent right here)
If you’re not funny,
it gets real serious here

23
00:00:46,046 --> 00:00:47,422
(Confident)
Yeah, I can be funny

24
00:00:47,422 --> 00:00:48,131
Rap

25
00:00:48,132 --> 00:00:49,799
Bout it, bout it,
all the way down to my toes, toes

26
00:00:49,799 --> 00:00:51,509
Get on the beat

27
00:00:51,509 --> 00:00:53,136
(Cold)
I don’t know the lyrics

28
00:00:53,722 --> 00:00:54,890
(Wow)

29
00:00:59,309 --> 00:01:04,439
(Is this really what it's like
being the Workdol MC..?.)

30
00:01:04,439 --> 00:01:05,857
(In awe)

31
00:01:05,857 --> 00:01:07,442
(Satisfied)
Yeah, like this

32
00:01:07,445 --> 00:01:09,445
(Nervous/ Nervous 22)
So today's part-time job is

33
00:01:09,445 --> 00:01:11,405
ice cream

34
00:01:11,949 --> 00:01:13,073
(Here to destroy their forearms)

35
00:01:13,865 --> 00:01:15,116
(Working at Baskin Robbins)

36
00:01:15,116 --> 00:01:17,077
(Already worried)
Since it’s such a big store,

37
00:01:17,077 --> 00:01:19,079
I’m thinking this might be

38
00:01:19,080 --> 00:01:20,080
a bit harder than usual

39
00:01:20,080 --> 00:01:21,915
You think it will be hard?

40
00:01:21,916 --> 00:01:22,957
It’s gonna be hella rough

41
00:01:22,958 --> 00:01:24,793
(Flustered)
Wait, is it okay to say "hella” on here?

42
00:01:24,793 --> 00:01:26,837
(It’s okay, guys...)
50 today

43
00:01:26,837 --> 00:01:30,299
(Because it actually is "hella" rough)
Feeling faint

44
00:01:30,299 --> 00:01:30,716
(Let's go to work)

45
00:01:30,716 --> 00:01:31,508
All right, let's go

46
00:01:31,508 --> 00:01:32,593
Go

47
00:01:34,094 --> 00:01:35,637
I’ve got some backup

48
00:01:35,637 --> 00:01:37,931
with me today,

49
00:01:37,932 --> 00:01:38,974
so I can take it easy

50
00:01:38,974 --> 00:01:41,560
(Finally entering)
Wow, it really is huge

51
00:01:42,898 --> 00:01:43,771
It’s really this nice?

52
00:01:43,771 --> 00:01:45,773
Where’s the mentor
we’ll be working with today?

53
00:01:45,773 --> 00:01:47,107
Sunbae!

54
00:01:47,107 --> 00:01:49,026
- Sunbae!
- Sunbae!

55
00:01:50,027 --> 00:01:51,320
Is it her here...?

56
00:01:52,904 --> 00:01:54,155
(Jihyun Lee/ 11th year)
Welcome

57
00:01:54,155 --> 00:01:55,198
Welcome to Baskin-Robbins

58
00:01:55,198 --> 00:01:56,366
(Baffled)
Hello

59
00:01:56,366 --> 00:01:57,367
Hello

60
00:01:57,367 --> 00:01:58,660
(Runs off immediately)
What was that entrance just now?

61
00:01:58,660 --> 00:02:00,870
(Shy woman)

62
00:02:00,870 --> 00:02:03,164
(Changed clothes)
I’m going to crush today’s part-time shift

63
00:02:03,164 --> 00:02:04,332
Are you ready?

64
00:02:05,292 --> 00:02:07,377
(Whoops)
Aaaaaah!

65
00:02:07,377 --> 00:02:09,289
(Looks like she’s about to
smash the camera first)

66
00:02:09,291 --> 00:02:10,421
Are you okay?

67
00:02:10,422 --> 00:02:11,047
(Shy)

68
00:02:11,048 --> 00:02:12,966
Trainees, please come in this way

69
00:02:12,966 --> 00:02:13,717
Yes!

70
00:02:13,717 --> 00:02:14,926
Super introvert

71
00:02:14,926 --> 00:02:16,762
She really is a super introvert

72
00:02:16,762 --> 00:02:17,971
We have to focus

73
00:02:17,971 --> 00:02:20,182
because her voice is

74
00:02:20,182 --> 00:02:22,642
ridiculously quiet

75
00:02:22,642 --> 00:02:24,353
(So quiet)
Please wear gloves

76
00:02:24,353 --> 00:02:25,729
(Splashing around)
We wear gloves?

77
00:02:25,729 --> 00:02:27,272
Oh, my face

78
00:02:27,272 --> 00:02:27,606
You

79
00:02:27,606 --> 00:02:28,815
(Pow)
can’t do that on my face

80
00:02:28,815 --> 00:02:30,442
It feels like a coming-of-age drama

81
00:02:31,193 --> 00:02:32,319
Hey

82
00:02:32,320 --> 00:02:34,571
(You little troublemaker)
Can’t you even put your gloves on?

83
00:02:34,571 --> 00:02:36,615
(A formidable opponent...)
I can already tell this is going to be tough

84
00:02:36,615 --> 00:02:38,867
(Already exhausted)

85
00:02:38,867 --> 00:02:41,495
I’m kind of excited
to work at Baskin-Robbins

86
00:02:41,496 --> 00:02:43,163
I heard it’s really intense

87
00:02:43,163 --> 00:02:44,790
(Dopamine addict)
That’s why I’m looking forward to it

88
00:02:45,999 --> 00:02:47,417
You’re actually looking forward to it?

89
00:02:47,417 --> 00:02:48,418
From what I’ve heard,

90
00:02:48,418 --> 00:02:50,503
the Rainbow Sherbet
doesn’t melt that easily

91
00:02:50,504 --> 00:02:51,797
Go ahead and try it right now

92
00:02:51,797 --> 00:02:53,132
Without a demonstration?

93
00:02:53,132 --> 00:02:55,050
(Checking it myself, brb)
Like a dung beetle rolling a ball?

94
00:02:56,176 --> 00:02:57,094
Wait a sec

95
00:02:57,094 --> 00:02:57,761
(Flustered)

96
00:02:57,761 --> 00:02:59,054
Why isn’t it working?

97
00:03:02,641 --> 00:03:05,269
(Totally freaked out)

98
00:03:05,269 --> 00:03:07,604
Sunbae, I’m kind of going for a gelato vibe

99
00:03:07,605 --> 00:03:09,523
No, seriously, it won’t come off!

100
00:03:09,523 --> 00:03:10,774
(Shocked)
Look at this

101
00:03:10,774 --> 00:03:12,276
(Trying to cover it)
It's art

102
00:03:12,276 --> 00:03:14,027
(Separating it)

103
00:03:14,027 --> 00:03:15,863
(Getting weirder and weirder)
No, seriously, it won’t come off

104
00:03:15,868 --> 00:03:18,115
If we just leave it
sitting there like this,

105
00:03:18,116 --> 00:03:19,575
people will come by and take pictures

106
00:03:20,367 --> 00:03:21,618
This is kind of art

107
00:03:21,619 --> 00:03:23,954
(The reality of modern art)
Modern art

108
00:03:23,954 --> 00:03:26,290
(Demonstration)
First, you have to shake the water off
the scoop

109
00:03:26,290 --> 00:03:28,250
(Single Scoop)
Shake off the excess water

110
00:03:28,251 --> 00:03:30,124
(2. Shape it)
After shaking off the excess water,
roll it into a half-moon shape

111
00:03:30,124 --> 00:03:31,753
Roll it into a half-moon

112
00:03:31,753 --> 00:03:34,298
(3. Place it in the cup)

113
00:03:34,298 --> 00:03:36,800
(Challenge)
You have to hold it like this

114
00:03:36,800 --> 00:03:37,926
Who are you talking to?

115
00:03:37,926 --> 00:03:40,220
Uh, it’s way too stiff

116
00:03:40,221 --> 00:03:41,386
(Endless practice begins)

117
00:03:41,386 --> 00:03:42,264
You got a feel to it

118
00:03:42,264 --> 00:03:44,308
You can do it

119
00:03:44,308 --> 00:03:47,060
This is just the beginning

120
00:03:47,060 --> 00:03:50,355
(Perfect)

121
00:03:50,355 --> 00:03:51,857
My first Baskin-Robbins ice cream

122
00:03:51,857 --> 00:03:53,233
(Huh?)
Perfect

123
00:03:53,233 --> 00:03:54,732
(No fake memories, please)

124
00:03:54,732 --> 00:03:56,069
Finally, finally

125
00:03:56,069 --> 00:03:59,531
(Next: pint practice)
With a pint, you get three flavors

126
00:03:59,531 --> 00:04:02,117
You scoop it in
so the customer can see all three

127
00:04:02,117 --> 00:04:05,162
Oh, you know how you kind of roll it
into a little ball like this?

128
00:04:05,162 --> 00:04:06,622
No

129
00:04:06,623 --> 00:04:07,539
(Firm)
Please focus

130
00:04:07,539 --> 00:04:10,500
(Focus)
Scrape along the wall

131
00:04:10,500 --> 00:04:12,878
This is hard to line up

132
00:04:12,879 --> 00:04:14,463
(Shaking)
Whoa, this is the one

133
00:04:14,463 --> 00:04:15,130
It's so stiff

134
00:04:15,130 --> 00:04:16,423
Yeah, this one’s stiff

135
00:04:16,424 --> 00:04:17,841
Guess this one isn’t popular

136
00:04:17,841 --> 00:04:19,927
The unpopular ones are
hard to scoop, right?

137
00:04:19,927 --> 00:04:21,470
(Cold)
No

138
00:04:21,471 --> 00:04:24,431
(So cold)
No sympathy at all

139
00:04:24,431 --> 00:04:26,350
(Exhausted)
Ugh, it’s hot

140
00:04:26,350 --> 00:04:27,893
But with this,

141
00:04:27,893 --> 00:04:31,021
if you’re pretty short, it might be tough

142
00:04:31,021 --> 00:04:33,231
Are Jiwon's feet floating again?

143
00:04:33,231 --> 00:04:34,358
(Checks right away)

144
00:04:34,358 --> 00:04:37,319
(On tiptoes, stepping down)
Your timing is so...

145
00:04:37,319 --> 00:04:39,321
(Didn’t get caught)
The timing is insane, right?

146
00:04:39,321 --> 00:04:41,490
(Missed the moment)

147
00:04:41,490 --> 00:04:43,367
I’ll give it a try

148
00:04:43,368 --> 00:04:45,077
(All swagger)

149
00:04:45,077 --> 00:04:46,620
She's walking like a gangster

150
00:04:46,620 --> 00:04:49,289
(Kind of intimidating)
This is seriously hilarious

151
00:04:49,289 --> 00:04:50,749
She's the Scoop serial killer

152
00:04:50,749 --> 00:04:52,793
(Looks like she’s about to
scoop away everything)
Like this

153
00:04:52,793 --> 00:04:55,379
(Sunbae)
You’re in a girl group

154
00:04:55,796 --> 00:04:57,715
(Glances over)

155
00:04:57,715 --> 00:04:59,591
(Getting dirty...?)

156
00:04:59,591 --> 00:05:01,218
Trying to look like you worked hard?

157
00:05:01,218 --> 00:05:02,720
How did you know?

158
00:05:02,720 --> 00:05:05,014
(You’re in a girl group too!)
How did you know?

159
00:05:05,014 --> 00:05:06,050
(12:00 PM
Open for business)

160
00:05:06,050 --> 00:05:10,144
Thank you. Enjoy your meal

161
00:05:10,144 --> 00:05:12,187
Jiwon and Rora will handle the scoops

162
00:05:12,187 --> 00:05:13,522
Chiquita and I will go run the counter

163
00:05:13,522 --> 00:05:15,190
(So sweet)

164
00:05:15,190 --> 00:05:16,442
(Bye)
Uh, go on

165
00:05:16,442 --> 00:05:17,943
Chiquita, you got this!

166
00:05:17,943 --> 00:05:19,486
She finally left

167
00:05:19,486 --> 00:05:21,780
(Finally, some peace and quiet)
She said she finally left

168
00:05:21,780 --> 00:05:25,451
(Practicing greetings)
Welcome, this is Baskin Robbins

169
00:05:25,451 --> 00:05:26,577
May I help

170
00:05:26,577 --> 00:05:27,786
with your order?

171
00:05:27,786 --> 00:05:28,454
Yes

172
00:05:28,454 --> 00:05:31,248
I’m so nervous I can’t get the words out

173
00:05:34,417 --> 00:05:37,170
(Customer walks in)
Welcome to Baskin-Robbins

174
00:05:37,170 --> 00:05:39,297
What size can I get you?

175
00:05:39,297 --> 00:05:41,674
Two Single Regulars, please

176
00:05:41,674 --> 00:05:45,094
(Nervous, but doing her job)
- Would you like it in a cup?
- In a cone, please

177
00:05:45,094 --> 00:05:47,430
I came in because I got so mad
my blood sugar dipped a bit

178
00:05:47,430 --> 00:05:49,015
Oh

179
00:05:49,015 --> 00:05:52,894
(Have some and calm down...)
Please choose. We’ve got lots of flavors

180
00:05:52,894 --> 00:05:53,811
(Nice to meet you)
Oh, hello! Welcome

181
00:05:53,813 --> 00:05:54,854
Hello there

182
00:05:54,854 --> 00:05:56,856
(First, an enthusiastic welcome)
This is Baskin-Robbins

183
00:05:56,856 --> 00:05:58,483
(Energy up)
Hello

184
00:05:58,483 --> 00:05:59,651
Hello

185
00:05:59,651 --> 00:06:01,319
She said she came
because her blood sugar dropped

186
00:06:01,319 --> 00:06:02,904
Oh, your blood sugar dropped

187
00:06:02,905 --> 00:06:04,364
(Dispensing sugar immediately)
Just a moment, please

188
00:06:04,364 --> 00:06:07,804
- Here you go. Enjoy
- Thank you

189
00:06:07,804 --> 00:06:09,369
I scooped that so well

190
00:06:09,369 --> 00:06:10,787
Are you two friends?

191
00:06:10,787 --> 00:06:12,580
No, she's my superior, and I’m below her

192
00:06:12,581 --> 00:06:13,957
(Staff/ Manager)

193
00:06:13,957 --> 00:06:15,291
Oh, really?

194
00:06:15,291 --> 00:06:17,335
What’s the vibe like? The company culture?

195
00:06:17,335 --> 00:06:20,964
Maybe because it’s a foreign-owned company,
things feel a bit more relaxed at work

196
00:06:20,964 --> 00:06:24,676
(Fantasy)
But if it’s a foreign company,
it’s usually pretty laid-back, right?

197
00:06:24,676 --> 00:06:25,718
Do you speak casually?

198
00:06:25,718 --> 00:06:27,637
(So proper)
No casual speech

199
00:06:27,637 --> 00:06:29,097
Wow, you’re really drawing a clear line

200
00:06:29,097 --> 00:06:30,598
Yep, this is definitely Korea

201
00:06:30,598 --> 00:06:32,016
(Blunt)
Casual-speech time starts now

202
00:06:32,016 --> 00:06:33,726
(All of a sudden...?)
Casual-speech time starts now

203
00:06:34,936 --> 00:06:36,354
Do you want a bite?

204
00:06:36,354 --> 00:06:38,898
(You wanna die?)
She seriously hates it

205
00:06:39,357 --> 00:06:40,608
(Startled)
Ah!

206
00:06:40,608 --> 00:06:43,987
(Second office-worker customer)
Welcome, this is Baskin-Robbins

207
00:06:43,987 --> 00:06:46,322
(Shy)
Please tell me what you need

208
00:06:46,322 --> 00:06:47,699
Whatever’s popular

209
00:06:47,699 --> 00:06:48,575
Whatever's popular?

210
00:06:48,575 --> 00:06:49,909
How are you feeling right now?

211
00:06:49,909 --> 00:06:52,328
(I’ll recommend something to match)
How are you feeling?

212
00:06:52,328 --> 00:06:53,872
These days, the world’s been rough,

213
00:06:53,873 --> 00:06:56,666
so I think we’re feeling it too

214
00:06:56,667 --> 00:07:00,003
If you have some ice cream,
you’ll feel so much better

215
00:07:00,003 --> 00:07:02,380
(No recommendation received)
Which flavor would you like?

216
00:07:02,380 --> 00:07:04,173
(Need sugar)
Just give me something sweet please

217
00:07:04,173 --> 00:07:06,926
(The reality for Korean office workers)
Office workers really do go
for sweet stuff a lot

218
00:07:06,927 --> 00:07:08,761
What do you do?

219
00:07:08,762 --> 00:07:10,263
I work at an insurance company

220
00:07:10,264 --> 00:07:11,264
Oh, insurance

221
00:07:11,264 --> 00:07:13,641
(One person looking especially exhausted...)
Insurance?

222
00:07:13,641 --> 00:07:15,184
(Worried)
Is your blood sugar really low?

223
00:07:15,184 --> 00:07:16,060
Yes

224
00:07:16,060 --> 00:07:17,228
Why is it low?

225
00:07:17,228 --> 00:07:18,897
What was so hard?

226
00:07:21,066 --> 00:07:23,110
A client asked me to throw away

227
00:07:23,110 --> 00:07:25,153
the trash they were holding when they left

228
00:07:25,695 --> 00:07:26,404
Oh my god

229
00:07:28,073 --> 00:07:30,492
They put their trash in my hand

230
00:07:30,493 --> 00:07:31,994
and then wiped their hand on mine once more

231
00:07:31,994 --> 00:07:33,054
(Met a trash of a client)

232
00:07:33,055 --> 00:07:34,939
- That’s a bit...
- That one’s a total nightmare customer

233
00:07:34,939 --> 00:07:36,664
No, seriously, that’s not okay

234
00:07:36,664 --> 00:07:38,666
(Public shaming, let’s go)
A word for that nightmare client

235
00:07:38,667 --> 00:07:39,125
(PTSD)

236
00:07:39,125 --> 00:07:40,751
I’m sweating like crazy

237
00:07:40,752 --> 00:07:42,670
Just thinking about it
makes me break out in a sweat

238
00:07:42,670 --> 00:07:44,129
Please don’t harass us

239
00:07:44,130 --> 00:07:46,341
(Refreshing)
Please. Thank you

240
00:07:46,341 --> 00:07:49,719
(Are you watching, you pain in the ass?)
- Don’t bully them, you jerks
- This is brutal

241
00:07:49,719 --> 00:07:50,928
(New order)
They want it packed in a quart size

242
00:07:50,928 --> 00:07:52,388
A quart-size cup

243
00:07:52,847 --> 00:07:54,015
Ugh

244
00:07:54,015 --> 00:07:56,434
(Hard)
Some of this stuff
just won’t get scooped, you know

245
00:07:56,435 --> 00:07:58,353
(Pressing with all her might)
And

246
00:07:58,353 --> 00:08:01,647
- The New York cheesecake is good too
- New York style

247
00:08:01,647 --> 00:08:03,316
Enjoy your meal

248
00:08:03,316 --> 00:08:04,108
Enjoy

249
00:08:04,109 --> 00:08:06,236
Goodbye

250
00:08:06,236 --> 00:08:07,988
Here you go

251
00:08:07,988 --> 00:08:09,698
(Customers kept pouring in...)
Enjoy your meal

252
00:08:09,698 --> 00:08:11,241
I’ll start with “Mom Is an Alien” first

253
00:08:11,241 --> 00:08:14,328
You’re the lucky winner, ma'am

254
00:08:14,911 --> 00:08:18,623
(Bulking up her forearms)

255
00:08:18,623 --> 00:08:20,333
(Zoned out)
Wait, what is this?

256
00:08:21,793 --> 00:08:23,044
Looks like a big group just came in

257
00:08:23,044 --> 00:08:25,171
(Tired)

258
00:08:25,172 --> 00:08:27,632
(Next customer, no time to breathe)
It’s Baskin-Robbins

259
00:08:27,632 --> 00:08:30,385
(Why is everyone so tall...)
- Hello
- Hello, this is Baskin-Robbins

260
00:08:30,385 --> 00:08:31,720
What do you all do?

261
00:08:31,720 --> 00:08:32,595
We work as models

262
00:08:32,595 --> 00:08:33,972
Knew it

263
00:08:33,972 --> 00:08:37,517
(Made on the spot)
Oh, don’t you think
I’m pretty good at this?

264
00:08:37,517 --> 00:08:41,062
(Quick sugar boost)
What else would you like to eat?

265
00:08:41,062 --> 00:08:42,314
I've never seen a celebrity before

266
00:08:42,314 --> 00:08:43,064
Me neither

267
00:08:43,064 --> 00:08:44,607
(Celebrity)
So, what do you think?

268
00:08:44,607 --> 00:08:47,360
Who do you like better?

269
00:08:49,696 --> 00:08:52,532
- Today’s not going to be easy
- Thank you

270
00:08:52,532 --> 00:08:55,201
What are you doing? Aren’t you working?

271
00:08:55,202 --> 00:08:55,994
There’s no work

272
00:08:55,994 --> 00:08:57,370
Then sing me a song, quick

273
00:08:57,371 --> 00:09:03,460
(Shows off their talent out of nowhere)

274
00:09:04,544 --> 00:09:06,421
- Scream, scream
- Ugh, this is exhausting

275
00:09:06,421 --> 00:09:07,756
Oooohhhhh

276
00:09:07,756 --> 00:09:10,425
(All done with the group order)
- Enjoy your meal
- Thank you

277
00:09:10,425 --> 00:09:12,218
(Shorty)
Wow, those people are seriously

278
00:09:12,218 --> 00:09:13,887
So tall

279
00:09:13,887 --> 00:09:15,930
I looked up at them like this

280
00:09:15,930 --> 00:09:17,432
Ugh, my back hurts

281
00:09:17,432 --> 00:09:19,517
(Hurting from all the looking up)

282
00:09:19,517 --> 00:09:22,645
(After lunch, the store quiets down)
- Let’s take a quick break
- Sure

283
00:09:22,645 --> 00:09:24,022
(Bored)

284
00:09:24,022 --> 00:09:25,899
Shouldn’t we be out there
drumming up some business?

285
00:09:25,899 --> 00:09:29,069
We’ve got way too few customers.
It’s a ghost town

286
00:09:32,322 --> 00:09:34,291
(Soliciting at the window)

287
00:09:34,291 --> 00:09:35,366
Come on in!

288
00:09:35,367 --> 00:09:35,659
(Spots someone)

289
00:09:35,659 --> 00:09:37,869
Uh, excuse me, sir!

290
00:09:37,870 --> 00:09:40,205
(Where's she going again...?)

291
00:09:40,997 --> 00:09:42,499
Wow, wow, wow!

292
00:09:42,499 --> 00:09:43,833
Seriously, respect

293
00:09:43,833 --> 00:09:45,877
Now that’s how you do it
as a Workdol MC

294
00:09:45,878 --> 00:09:49,339
(Soliciting in full force)

295
00:09:49,339 --> 00:09:51,591
(Ignoring her)
COME, COME

296
00:09:51,591 --> 00:09:54,302
Nobody's coming

297
00:09:54,302 --> 00:09:55,887
Totally ignored

298
00:09:55,887 --> 00:09:56,471
(Thud)

299
00:09:56,471 --> 00:09:57,222
Oh man

300
00:09:57,222 --> 00:09:58,723
Oh man, oh man

301
00:09:59,265 --> 00:10:01,392
Spring fever's hitting me

302
00:10:01,392 --> 00:10:03,853
(Why are you suddenly
getting spring fever...?)

303
00:10:03,853 --> 00:10:04,937
We’ve got an order coming in

304
00:10:04,937 --> 00:10:05,480
Oh, it’s in

305
00:10:05,480 --> 00:10:07,440
Sunbae, time to get to work

306
00:10:07,440 --> 00:10:10,401
Wait, what? An order just came in?

307
00:10:10,401 --> 00:10:12,779
(A customer comes in too)
Welcome to Baskin-Robbins

308
00:10:12,779 --> 00:10:14,781
Hi, I’ll help you with your order here

309
00:10:14,781 --> 00:10:17,700
Personally, I like "Mom Is an Alien"

310
00:10:17,700 --> 00:10:18,743
Just one of those, please

311
00:10:18,743 --> 00:10:20,077
Okay, got it

312
00:10:20,077 --> 00:10:21,621
What do you do for work?

313
00:10:21,621 --> 00:10:24,999
I’m working part-time
at the Chinese restaurant next door

314
00:10:24,999 --> 00:10:26,292
How is it. Hard?

315
00:10:26,292 --> 00:10:28,294
Yeah, the trash comes in

316
00:10:28,294 --> 00:10:30,087
really heavy for us

317
00:10:30,087 --> 00:10:31,422
Hey, hey, hey!

318
00:10:31,422 --> 00:10:33,382
That difficult customer is about to leave

319
00:10:33,382 --> 00:10:34,884
A difficult customer?

320
00:10:34,884 --> 00:10:36,969
Could it be some entitled customer?

321
00:10:36,969 --> 00:10:37,637
No, just someone whose blood sugar’s low

322
00:10:37,637 --> 00:10:38,971
Ohhh

323
00:10:38,971 --> 00:10:41,766
(Pumps the energy back up)
Hello, welcome to Baskin-Robbins

324
00:10:41,766 --> 00:10:43,434
(Wearing Chinese-restaurant attire)
Do you work at a Chinese restaurant?

325
00:10:43,435 --> 00:10:44,435
Yes, that’s right

326
00:10:44,435 --> 00:10:46,896
I’ve actually done part-time work
at a Chinese restaurant too

327
00:10:46,897 --> 00:10:47,688
I watched it

328
00:10:47,688 --> 00:10:49,357
You got so many mean comments

329
00:10:49,358 --> 00:10:50,066
Ahem

330
00:10:50,066 --> 00:10:53,069
(Caught off guard)
I did get some flak for being bad at my job

331
00:10:53,069 --> 00:10:55,279
If you’d gone out on your own,
I bet you would’ve done really well

332
00:10:55,280 --> 00:10:56,322
(Fair)
Yes

333
00:10:56,322 --> 00:10:57,698
I’m front-of-house material

334
00:10:57,698 --> 00:10:59,325
(Born for the service industry)

335
00:10:59,325 --> 00:11:01,786
(Cheongdam Street)
And isn’t that place luxurious, too?

336
00:11:01,786 --> 00:11:03,329
If it’s expensive, you’ve got to treat them

337
00:11:03,329 --> 00:11:05,206
really well, right?

338
00:11:05,206 --> 00:11:07,750
(Order’s up)
What kind of clientele do you usually get?

339
00:11:07,750 --> 00:11:09,961
Usually it’s some chairman type

340
00:11:09,961 --> 00:11:12,004
(Chairman stereotype)
And sometimes, when they’re drunk,

341
00:11:12,004 --> 00:11:13,631
they’ll leave a 50,000-won tip

342
00:11:13,631 --> 00:11:15,466
(A 50,000-won tip...?)

343
00:11:15,466 --> 00:11:16,425
Here, take this for the cab fare

344
00:11:16,425 --> 00:11:17,301
Oh my

345
00:11:17,301 --> 00:11:18,511
One more?

346
00:11:18,511 --> 00:11:19,929
(Yeah)
Yellow, yellow one?

347
00:11:19,930 --> 00:11:21,722
(Adding another tip...)
And then they'd give me more,
thinking they didn't give me one

348
00:11:21,722 --> 00:11:24,433
(This is getting interesting)
- Then, then. Wait a second
- "I didn't take it!"

349
00:11:24,433 --> 00:11:25,935
Wait, then

350
00:11:25,935 --> 00:11:28,062
you can wear glasses,

351
00:11:28,062 --> 00:11:29,188
take it off, and then

352
00:11:29,188 --> 00:11:29,939
tie your hair

353
00:11:29,939 --> 00:11:31,232
Hello

354
00:11:31,232 --> 00:11:34,193
(Endless tip refills)
Hair tied up like this. Hello!

355
00:11:34,193 --> 00:11:35,695
(Still greeting customers...)
Welcome in!

356
00:11:35,695 --> 00:11:38,155
Welcome to Baskin-Robbins!

357
00:11:38,156 --> 00:11:42,076
(Giving it my all at customer service)
Hello!

358
00:11:42,076 --> 00:11:45,037
This customer’s here for a sugar fix!

359
00:11:45,037 --> 00:11:48,291
(Sugar replenished, done)
Enjoy your treat, enjoy your treat!

360
00:11:48,291 --> 00:11:51,961
(Another customer)
I’m going to hand off
the customer who’s been slacking

361
00:11:51,962 --> 00:11:53,087
(Exhausted)

362
00:11:53,088 --> 00:11:55,046
This is rough

363
00:11:55,048 --> 00:11:57,592
(Trying hard)

364
00:12:00,428 --> 00:12:02,722
Rora, you look totally worn out

365
00:12:02,723 --> 00:12:03,765
Rora, are you okay?

366
00:12:03,765 --> 00:12:06,142
(That forced energy is obvious...)
What are you talking about?

367
00:12:06,142 --> 00:12:08,728
(Taking a break)
Looks like working
the counter really wiped you out

368
00:12:08,729 --> 00:12:12,231
(Exhausted...)
That’s the eyebrow you make
when things are really tough

369
00:12:12,231 --> 00:12:14,192
(Quick check)
Hang on,

370
00:12:14,193 --> 00:12:15,943
how long are we working today?

371
00:12:15,943 --> 00:12:17,820
We’ve got 25 minutes left until clock-out

372
00:12:17,820 --> 00:12:19,781
Yes!

373
00:12:19,781 --> 00:12:22,116
No, you really spilled it

374
00:12:22,116 --> 00:12:27,372
(Everyone hustles...)

375
00:12:27,372 --> 00:12:30,541
How was it?
Your ice cream shop shift today?

376
00:12:30,542 --> 00:12:32,794
It was rough

377
00:12:32,794 --> 00:12:34,295
Totally brutal

378
00:12:34,295 --> 00:12:36,589
Ugh, I'm wiped

379
00:12:36,589 --> 00:12:38,591
(Peek)

380
00:12:38,591 --> 00:12:40,843
How long until we get off work?

381
00:12:40,843 --> 00:12:41,803
About five minutes left

382
00:12:41,803 --> 00:12:43,680
(Excited)
Oh yeah, oh yeeeaaah!

383
00:12:43,680 --> 00:12:45,598
(Happy)

384
00:12:45,598 --> 00:12:48,101
(Back to work)
I'll make you a theme song with Chiquita

385
00:12:48,101 --> 00:12:51,646
(Cheerful because it’s almost time to clock out)
Spin guitar to the Chiquita rhythm

386
00:12:51,646 --> 00:12:52,605
Spin guitar to the Chiquita rhythm

387
00:12:52,605 --> 00:12:54,941
(No HP)

388
00:12:54,941 --> 00:12:55,483
(A customer comes in)

389
00:12:55,483 --> 00:12:56,401
Customer!

390
00:12:56,401 --> 00:12:57,527
Oh, the counter

391
00:12:57,527 --> 00:12:58,820
Hello

392
00:12:58,820 --> 00:13:00,113
Fifty single cups,

393
00:13:00,113 --> 00:13:01,354
please

394
00:13:01,354 --> 00:13:03,199
Fifty single cups?

395
00:13:03,200 --> 00:13:04,951
Fifty cups?

396
00:13:04,951 --> 00:13:07,286
Hold on, the last customer is
way too intense

397
00:13:07,286 --> 00:13:08,871
Fifty?

398
00:13:08,871 --> 00:13:13,251
(Death glare)
Sunbaes, we’ve got a group order,
50 single cups

399
00:13:13,251 --> 00:13:15,837
(Zen mode)
I’ll scoop it out
with all the love I’ve got

400
00:13:15,837 --> 00:13:17,714
How about a Shooting Star?

401
00:13:17,714 --> 00:13:19,006
Oh, Shooting Star. Nice

402
00:13:20,091 --> 00:13:21,134
Wait, what?

403
00:13:21,134 --> 00:13:23,511
I think I’ve genuinely gotten better

404
00:13:23,845 --> 00:13:25,847
(Perfect form)
I think I nailed that one
the most perfectly

405
00:13:25,847 --> 00:13:28,183
(Can’t lose)
Don’t you think I’m actually pretty good?

406
00:13:28,183 --> 00:13:30,477
(Might as well get hired)
This shape is insane

407
00:13:30,477 --> 00:13:32,145
Who is it for?

408
00:13:32,145 --> 00:13:33,563
We're going to meet club friends

409
00:13:33,563 --> 00:13:34,856
Are you two a couple, by any chance?

410
00:13:34,856 --> 00:13:35,690
Yeah

411
00:13:35,690 --> 00:13:37,650
(Seriously...)

412
00:13:37,651 --> 00:13:41,321
(Let’s just focus on work...)
Apple Mint

413
00:13:41,321 --> 00:13:43,740
This one takes a bit more effort

414
00:13:43,740 --> 00:13:45,075
(The end)
Ahh, I’m finally done

415
00:13:45,075 --> 00:13:46,826
Oooooooooh!

416
00:13:46,826 --> 00:13:49,746
Who was the one to confess first?

417
00:13:49,747 --> 00:13:50,914
(I went first)
I was the one who confessed

418
00:13:50,914 --> 00:13:53,083
Woooow!

419
00:13:53,083 --> 00:13:54,042
You worked up the nerve

420
00:13:54,042 --> 00:13:55,335
How did you do it?

421
00:13:55,335 --> 00:13:58,088
My girlfriend was meeting a friend,

422
00:13:58,088 --> 00:14:00,715
so I went to pick her up and confessed
in front of her place at night

423
00:14:00,715 --> 00:14:02,592
So you basically told her to get in the car

424
00:14:02,594 --> 00:14:03,176
Oh, right

425
00:14:03,176 --> 00:14:04,927
I did that in Gangnam

426
00:14:04,927 --> 00:14:07,221
“Oppa got a new car”

427
00:14:07,221 --> 00:14:11,267
(Oppa is really drunk...)
“Oppa got a new car.
I'm coming to pick you up”

428
00:14:11,267 --> 00:14:13,102
(4:00 PM
Getting off work)
We're done

429
00:14:15,563 --> 00:14:17,065
We're heading home now

430
00:14:17,065 --> 00:14:18,775
Let me off

431
00:14:18,775 --> 00:14:22,945
(Paycheck from the part-time job)

432
00:14:22,945 --> 00:14:25,406
You all did great.
Seriously, everyone worked so hard

433
00:14:25,406 --> 00:14:27,366
Whoa, how much is it?

434
00:14:27,366 --> 00:14:28,367
300 won?

435
00:14:28,367 --> 00:14:29,660
41,300 won?

436
00:14:29,662 --> 00:14:30,828
(Baskin-Robbins payout = Total 41,300 won)
How many hours did we work today?

437
00:14:30,828 --> 00:14:34,582
4 hours. Hourly pay is 10,320 won

438
00:14:34,582 --> 00:14:36,793
(Dead-eyed)
That’s not too much

439
00:14:36,793 --> 00:14:38,670
That’s reasonable

440
00:14:39,837 --> 00:14:41,797
(So reasonable...)

441
00:14:41,797 --> 00:14:43,591
(Q. What was the toughest part?)
What was the hardest thing for you?

442
00:14:43,591 --> 00:14:45,301
At the counter, constantly going,

443
00:14:45,302 --> 00:14:46,594
“Welcome!”

444
00:14:46,594 --> 00:14:47,011
and keeping that kind of energy up

445
00:14:47,011 --> 00:14:48,262
Oh, like being bright and cheerful

446
00:14:48,262 --> 00:14:48,804
Cheerful

447
00:14:48,804 --> 00:14:52,183
(My face almost cramped up)
I smiled so much

448
00:14:52,183 --> 00:14:53,225
For me, the hardest part was

449
00:14:53,226 --> 00:14:55,269
scooping mint chocolate chip

450
00:14:55,269 --> 00:14:56,645
It just wouldn’t budge

451
00:14:56,646 --> 00:14:59,098
- It sticks to the scoop and won’t come off
- Apparently that’s a thing

452
00:14:59,098 --> 00:15:00,900
That one was the hardest

453
00:15:00,900 --> 00:15:02,860
(Heartbroken)
Don’t eat

454
00:15:02,860 --> 00:15:05,154
(Just get chocolate)
Don’t order mint chocolate

455
00:15:05,154 --> 00:15:07,573
I had no idea it was this hard

456
00:15:07,573 --> 00:15:09,158
I totally respect you guys

457
00:15:09,158 --> 00:15:12,453
(Shout-out to part-timers)
- Much respect
- Seriously, mad respect

458
00:15:12,453 --> 00:15:14,205
Working together today

459
00:15:14,210 --> 00:15:15,873
was fun, but

460
00:15:15,873 --> 00:15:18,793
(Hurting for the working man)
listening to his story was so sad

461
00:15:18,793 --> 00:15:19,960
They work so hard,

462
00:15:19,960 --> 00:15:22,003
and those rude customers, seriously...

463
00:15:22,004 --> 00:15:22,963
That's no good

464
00:15:22,963 --> 00:15:25,174
Rude customers need to
reflect on themselves

465
00:15:25,174 --> 00:15:27,843
(They’re all someone’s precious children...)
Please treat them kindly

466
00:15:27,843 --> 00:15:29,803
(BABYMONSTER’s surprise confession)

467
00:15:29,803 --> 00:15:32,714
(6 PM, May 4 - Baemon "CHOOM” comeback)
We’re making our comeback in May
with the title track "CHOOM”

468
00:15:32,714 --> 00:15:33,890
“CHOOM?”

469
00:15:33,891 --> 00:15:36,852
We’ve got a world tour in June

470
00:15:36,852 --> 00:15:38,938
It’s our second world tour

471
00:15:38,938 --> 00:15:41,482
(Promo over)
Let’s head out like this, guys

472
00:15:44,277 --> 00:15:45,987
(Let me off work)

473
00:15:45,989 --> 00:15:47,947
(A sunbae’s real-world advice)

474
00:15:47,947 --> 00:15:49,908
Is there anyone in BABYMONSTER

475
00:15:49,908 --> 00:15:52,619
who seems like
they’d be good at a part-time job?

476
00:15:52,619 --> 00:15:55,955
- First off, there’s a friend named Rora
- Really?

477
00:15:55,955 --> 00:15:58,708
She’s seriously sharp and capable

478
00:15:58,708 --> 00:15:59,959
But among the youngest ones,

479
00:15:59,959 --> 00:16:01,503
there’s a girl named Chiquita

480
00:16:01,503 --> 00:16:04,089
She doesn't really understand hierarchy,

481
00:16:04,089 --> 00:16:05,256
so even though I’m older,

482
00:16:05,257 --> 00:16:09,427
(Hierarchy in shambles)
she says we’re the same age just because
it’s only a six-month difference

483
00:16:09,427 --> 00:16:11,763
You can tell at a glance I’m the older one

484
00:16:11,763 --> 00:16:13,848
(Cut this)
I mean, it’s not even a full year

485
00:16:13,848 --> 00:16:16,601
Just six months, you know?

486
00:16:16,602 --> 00:16:18,853
Then, aren't we the same age?

487
00:16:18,857 --> 00:16:19,854
Ooooh

488
00:16:19,854 --> 00:16:23,065
Hey, how many years were you a trainee?

489
00:16:23,068 --> 00:16:24,859
(How should I know?)
I don't know

490
00:16:24,859 --> 00:16:26,152
How many years was it for me?

491
00:16:26,153 --> 00:16:26,694
You?

492
00:16:26,694 --> 00:16:27,987
There's a six year difference

493
00:16:27,987 --> 00:16:29,405
Did I do one year?

494
00:16:29,405 --> 00:16:31,324
None of it mattered

495
00:16:31,324 --> 00:16:34,369
If you just get out there,
work hard, and do well,

496
00:16:34,369 --> 00:16:37,205
it doesn’t matter whether you were
a trainee for a year, a few months,

497
00:16:37,205 --> 00:16:40,333
eight years, or six years

498
00:16:40,333 --> 00:16:43,503
(Reached nirvana)
It all ends up not mattering

499
00:16:43,505 --> 00:16:44,587
(Next week)
Let’s go check it out

500
00:16:44,587 --> 00:16:46,339
Catch me. PICK ME

501
00:16:46,339 --> 00:16:48,925
(On-foot debut coming soon)

